%description:
The TR 38.901 rural macrocell NLOS path loss takes log10(W) of the average street width W: at
W = 0 m it is -inf, and the path loss of an NLOS link +inf. A street width of 0 m or less is an
error on the first evaluation of a link of the cell, LOS or not, whatever
tolerateHeightViolation says.

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
network = simu5g.test.moduletest.lib.NrSessionTestNetwork

# a rural macrocell (TR 38.901 RMa), whose path loss takes the building height and street width
*.gnb.cellularNic.radio.scenario = "RURAL_MACROCELL"
*.gnb.cellularNic.radio.streetWidth = 0m
**.nrChannelModel[*].tolerateHeightViolation = true

include ../../lib/defaults.ini

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%exitcode: 1
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: stderr
the cell's building height is 5 m and its street width 0 m (the buildingHeight and streetWidth of its base station's radio), and the path loss of the scenario RURAL_MACROCELL takes their logarithms: both must be above 0 m
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
